          "reply_count": 5,
          "retweet_count": 8
        },
        "referenced_tweets": [
          {
            "id": "2075218936266998230",
            "type": "quoted"
          }
        ],
        "text": "We’re one step closer to our mission @alexandr_wang : Personal Superintelligence to everyone! It’s a rewarding process to build up the full-stack agent RL from container services of the monorepo, data to agentic RL/sampling algorithm together with the talents. We are https://t.co/7baL1gEg4v"
      },
      {
        "author_id": "267078542",
        "created_at": "2026-07-09T17:42:31.000Z",
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "2075274414149546146"
        ],
        "id": "2075274414149546146",
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 4,
          "impression_count": 36415,
          "like_count": 17,
          "quote_count": 1,
          "reply_count": 5,
          "retweet_count": 2
        },
        "referenced_tweets": [
          {
            "id": "2075218936266998230",
            "type": "quoted"
          }
        ],
        "text": "Muse Spark 1.1 seems like a very good model. I tested it on Stata Benchmark and it ranks 4th (!) beating Opus 4.7/4.8, tied with GPT 5.5. \n\nI like this benchmark because it often catches seemingly good model performing poorly on OOD tasks https://t.co/XNBL0EPEo6 https://t.co/X29ZW1Lmyv"
      },
